# Allowlist strategy: ignore everything at the root of ~/.claude, then opt in
# deliberately. New runtime/cache files from future Claude Code updates stay
# invisible by default — nothing leaks unless explicitly un-ignored below.
#
# The leading slash anchors to the repo root, so these patterns ignore ONLY
# top-level entries. Contents of re-included directories (memory/, skills/) are
# NOT ignored, because we never excluded anything inside them.
#
# NOTE: gitignore has no trailing/inline comments — a '#' only starts a comment
# at the START of a line. Keep every pattern on its own bare line.

/*

# --- opt back in (each on its own line, no trailing comments) ---

# global mentor instructions
!/CLAUDE.md
# shared config (NOT settings.local.json — that stays machine-local)
!/settings.json
# status line script
!/statusline.sh
# hook scripts referenced from settings.json (session-start ledger state) + fixture tests
!/hooks/
# validators, secret scan, packaging
!/scripts/
# custom slash commands (if present)
!/commands/
# global learning ledger
!/memory/
# mentor skill state: plans, journals, lessons per project
!/mentor/
# hand-made skills (mentor, teach, ...)
!/skills/
# design docs and specs
!/docs/
# repo map and review views
!/README.md
# this file
!/.gitignore

# --- never, even inside opted-in directories ---
# Claude Code's downloaded copy of Anthropic's built-in skills (docx, pptx, pdf, ...).
# Re-synced on every start; not ours, not hand-made.
/skills/synced/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.orig
*.swp
# packaged shareable zip (built by scripts/package-shareable.sh)
/claude-config-shareable.zip
# private state that must stay local even if a future split creates it next to this repo
/claude-state-private/

# Explicitly NOT tracked (sensitive / machine-local / churn) — already covered
# by /* above, listed here only as documentation of intent:
#   projects/             full conversation transcripts (mode 700) — secrets, code
#   history.jsonl         raw prompt history (mode 600)
#   file-history/         backups of edited files
#   plugins/              re-installable bulk
#   settings.local.json   machine-local overrides
#   cache/ backups/ paste-cache/ shell-snapshots/ sessions/ session-env/
#   daemon* tasks/ jobs/ stats-cache.json   runtime state
